        "original_id": "c8a35b7a-6bfe-51fa-9650-7b9078f199dc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Ships: San Juan de Sicilia\n- Fleets: Spanish Armada\n- People: Duke of Medina Sidonia\n- Places: La Coruña, Flanders, England\n- Events: Spanish Armada campaign of 1588\n\nFacts:\n- The Spanish Armada, also called the \"Grande y Felicísima Armada\" or \"Great and Most Fortunate Navy,\" was a Spanish fleet of 130 ships.\n- In August 1588, the Spanish Armada sailed from La Coruña under the command of the Duke of Medina Sidonia.\n- In 1588, the Spanish Armada aimed to escort an army from Flanders to invade England.\n- In 1588, the San Juan de Sicilia was one of the 130 ships in the ill-fated Spanish Armada.",
